A||||9||ounmongk||Anyone with BAZOOKA tubes? I need a bit of info... ||||1||
Z||000000||ounmongk||07-24-2000||02:59 PM||||How did you all mount the tube in your car? I have an 8". I'm going to try mounting it length-wise in the passenger footwell. Any better suggestions? TIA. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||07-24-2000||03:08 PM||||I have installed an 8 inch under the dash in the stock location. I had to cut it down to about 6 1/2 inches then reinstall the woofer <BR>It sounds really sweet!!<BR>LOOK!! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jul18^04.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jul18^07.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000002||rockcrawl||07-24-2000||05:27 PM||||Hi,<BR> I had a 6 (or is it 6.5) inch bazooka mounted like you said, on the passenger side floor, firing toward the footwell. It was strapped down using the staps that come with it. It wasn't really in the way for passengers. The only problem is that it is clearly visible to theifs.<P>------------------<BR>'86 GT 3800<BR>'87 GT<BR>Rossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||07-24-2000||05:37 PM||||As soon as I get around to it, I'll install two 5.25" Bazooka bass tubes behind each seat in my 86SE. They fit perfectly, and since I'm only 5'6" on a good day,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I don't lose any foot space!<BR>I'll have the tubes running off a Punch 45, and I'll install a full Alpine system as well. <P>The pair was only $100, and I'm sure they're going to sound sweet!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||jbarnes||07-24-2000||07:00 PM||||I have 2 8's behind the passenger. It sounds fantastic but since you only have one and bass is reported to sound better coming from the front (allbeit non-directional) maybe the footwell is best.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||07-25-2000||02:27 AM||||I have the 6.5" Powered (80W) Bazooka tube mounted behind the passenger seat. It sounds great for a 6.5" woofer.||||reg||1
Z||000006||pHoOl||07-26-2000||01:23 AM||||any suggestions for a 6'2" person who carts people around who are around the same height?  did i mention low cost?  or should i just keep dreaming?||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||07-26-2000||08:01 AM||||My suggestion is to avoid the Bazooka and make your own fiberglass enclosure for the passenger footwell. I run a 10" Polk sub in mine, hits great, and even at 6'6"I am able to fit comfortably in the passenger seat. I should have pics of my sub by this weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000008||ounmongk||07-26-2000||01:48 PM||||COOL! Thanks for all the info everyone! Feiro64: NICE! how did you mount that up there? Thanks again. <BR>Ohm ||||reg||1
Z||000009||TheFiero64||07-26-2000||05:21 PM||||Actually it is just sitting there. I stuck the leg on the tube under the carpet. On a BAZOOKA it would have to be strapped or a bracket would have to be fabricated. I lucked out on mine.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
